# Three teammates, three continents. When can all three take a call
# without anyone being up at midnight? Define each person's waking hours
# in THEIR zone, intersect, and read the answer in every zone at once.
#
# `in` takes a list: one stretch, three lenses, one card — a row per city.
# One instant, three wall times — the thing raw code always fumbles.

span = 2026-09-15 .. 2026-09-15          # a single day to search

timezone = America/Los_Angeles
sf  = every day 07:00 .. 22:00
timezone = Europe/London
ldn = every day 07:00 .. 22:00
timezone = Asia/Kolkata
blr = every day 07:00 .. 22:00

# the hours all three are awake, on that day
window = (sf & span) & (ldn & span) & (blr & span)

show window in America/Los_Angeles, Europe/London, Asia/Kolkata
#  → 07:00–09:30 breakfast in SF · 15:00–17:30 afternoon in London · 19:30–22:00 evening in Bangalore
